:{},"details":{"description":"<p>A ghostly pair of teenagers-the Xarwin twins-cry out in pain as their brains are replaced into their heads. As if their trauma reverses, the initial pain fades and they express the desire to play.</p>","disable":"<p>@Check[performance|dc:21|name:Distract the Haunt] (trained) to distract the haunt and entertain it until it becomes soothed or @Check[religion|dc:25|name:Exorcise Haunt] (trained) to exorcise the haunt</p>","isComplex":true,"level":{"value":6},"publication":{"license":"OGL","remaster":false,"title":"Pathfinder Adventure: Malevolence"},"reset":"<p>The haunt resets automatically 1 hour after it's defeated or after no living creatures remain in the area to play with. Removing Marney's and Mira's brains from the brain collector statue in area E9 destroys the haunt.</p>","routine":"<p>(2 actions) The architect (Mira Xarwin) uses Shackled Memories to cause a strange, house-like cage of solid ectoplasm to spring up around a randomly determined target. This house bears an uncanny resemblance to the home the target grew up in. The hunter (Marney Xarwin) then attempts a hunting shot Strike at that target.</p>"},"saves":{"fortitude":{"saveDetail":"","value":11},"reflex":{"saveDetail":"","value":17},"will":{"saveDetail":"","value":15}},"statusEffects":[],"traits":{"rarity":"common","size":{"value":"med"},"value":["haunt"]},"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"hazard","effects":[]},{"_id":"JMXNSC7M2SRGZbhy","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/npc.svg","items":["2hOUtgCM9lj7z4TB","wIfegH9lKXPcfiA2","SqGN2C6WwW664mJx","wsEjPohcBZ0DGWS5","zDmN2GNIClzY8q9J","CDTtHeFOvz7H1Jqo","MMSZxMrXIdeCFlFq"],"name":"Undead Brain Collector","system":{"abilities":{"cha":{"mod":0},"con":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":3},"int":{"mod":-1},"str":{"mod":6},"wis":{"mod":4}},"attributes":{"ac":{"details":"","value":24},"allSaves":{"value":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"hp":{"details":"void healing","max":130,"temp":0,"value":130},"immuniti